cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these data or this code, please cite the papers below."
title: "Heilbronn discovery lab: papers, certificates and verification code"
abstract: "Three papers on the Heilbronn triangle problem in the unit square with data and code: a computer-assisted proof that the known 9-point configuration is optimal, H(9) = (9 sqrt(65) - 55)/320 (code written with AI assistance, Claude, Anthropic; not yet independently checked), certificates for best-known configurations for n = 37-100, and a study of critical triangles."
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Hendren
    given-names: Ethan
license: [MIT, CC-BY-4.0]
date-released: 2026-11-12
keywords: [Heilbronn triangle problem, discrete geometry, computer-assisted proof, interval arithmetic]
references:
